>> title: Blackened Salmon, Air Fryer
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: salmon, fish, air fryer, basket, cajun, blackened
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: blackened-salmon
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer salmon, blackened salmon in the air fryer, basket salmon, cajun air fryer salmon
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: narrow — 52°C (125°F) is medium-rare; by 63°C (145°F) the albumin squeezes out white between the flakes and nothing puts it back
>> washing-up: the basket, the plate the spice was pressed on

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. Time tracks thickness here, not weight.
The heat travels inward, so a thicker fillet is a longer cook at the same weight.

>> step: stir the blackening spice on a plate
Stir @sweet paprika{2%Tbs}, @garlic powder{2%tsp}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, @cayenne{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} together on a #plate{}.

>> step: press one face into it, spice side up
Press @salmon fillets{4}(6 oz / 170 g each, 1 1/2 in thick; skin on) into @&(~1)blackening spice{} on one face only.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 10–14 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)spiced fillets{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{12%min}, one layer and spice side up.

>> step: probe the thickest part at ten minutes — 52°C (125°F)
Probe @&(~1)salmon{} at the thickest part.

>> step: lemon over, straight out of the basket
Squeeze @lemon{1/2}(cut in wedges) over @&(~1)salmon{}.

>> step: Three credible sources give three finish temperatures — 52°C, 55°C and 63°C. This file cooks to 52°C and says whose.
Not a rounding difference. Three opinions about what cooked salmon is.
